{"id": "EUVD-2026-103891", "enisaUuid": "0afe99bf-8c20-3c8f-97ce-2195bef651d0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocteontx2-pf: Fix aura BPID assignment when CONFIG_DCB is enabled\n\nPreviously, BPID assignment under CONFIG_DCB assumed\n`queue_to_pfc_map` was always initialized. For SDP VFs this leads to\ninvalid memory access as it was not initialized.\n\nThis patch adds a NULL check for `queue_to_pfc_map` before\ndereferencing it. Also, simplifies the logic by always assigning a\ndefault BPID first, then conditionally overriding it if CONFIG_DCB is\nenabled and the map exists.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:25:59", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/59fbbded05e559675930fd521b8d62b72828b52d", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/056994563935e049093f100efaad7e63ad113814"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98806", "GHSA-jmhr-qgjx-cxxh"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "323331b3-3068-3d6f-9130-66148fa6cccf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "184fb40f731bd3353b0887731f7caba66609e9cd <056994563935e049093f100efaad7e63ad113814"}, {"id": "56f1b34e-882d-356b-b09c-a60b2d96d91a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "5bf78386-a5c0-3565-b057-a25511675674", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "83f8d2d1-b7d2-3a26-880d-5989c2ba5374", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "22079d5ae4a33679150f7de89f4107f4e0446886"}, {"id": "84dd4a2f-3433-3cad-8585-cfcad5c70660", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "c47f3eaa-e6bf-3ac4-9722-345bd120c7b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "184fb40f731bd3353b0887731f7caba66609e9cd <59fbbded05e559675930fd521b8d62b72828b52d"}, {"id": "c75097f1-f69f-36f3-b08e-3b28e5fc6b28", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14.9 <6.15"}, {"id": "cfafd64a-18c1-3d23-8e98-49fc2f54b91a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2a527879-4019-34d9-95dc-c8431deb75ae", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}